# Modfem Autos — environment configuration
#
# Deployed to Cloudflare Workers via OpenNext (@opennextjs/cloudflare).
#
# !! Where each value lives — read this before copying the file !!
# `npm run build:cf` compiles EVERY .env* file into the deployed Worker
# bundle, and in production applies .env / .env.local / .env.production /
# .env.production.local as runtime fallbacks. So:
#   - Production secrets: `npx wrangler secret put ...` only (below). Never
#     in any .env* file or in wrangler.jsonc.
#   - Local `next dev`: copy this file to .env.development.local (NOT
#     .env.local) — it's only applied in development mode, so production
#     never falls back to it.
#   - Local `npm run preview:cf` (the built Worker running in workerd):
#     secrets come from a .dev.vars file (wrangler's convention, gitignored),
#     e.g. a single line: ADMIN_SECRET=some-local-value
# `build:cf` runs scripts/check-cf-env.mjs first and refuses to build if a
# server secret is sitting in a file it would bake in.
#
# Deploying to Cloudflare — plug-and-play checklist:
#   1. npx wrangler login
#   2. npx wrangler secret put ADMIN_SECRET
#        (prompts for the value; use a long random string, different from
#        your local dev one)
#   3. npx wrangler secret put DATABASE_URL
#        (a POOLED Postgres URL — see the Database section. Without it the
#        Worker still runs, but on in-memory state only: it resets on every
#        cold start and isn't shared across isolates/regions, and the Worker
#        logs a warning saying so.)
#   4. Set NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL in wrangler.jsonc "vars" AND in the shell that
#      runs the build — Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* at build time and these
#      pages prerender statically, so the wrangler var alone can't change
#      canonical/OpenGraph URLs. For Cloudflare Workers Builds (Git-connected
#      CI), add it under the project's Build variables instead.
#        bash:        NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://modfemautos.com npm run build:cf
#        PowerShell:  $env:NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://modfemautos.com"; npm run build:cf
#   5. One-time database setup (shell-scoped DATABASE_URL, since it must not
#      live in any .env* file):
#        bash:        DATABASE_URL="postgres://..." npx prisma migrate dev --name init
#        PowerShell:  $env:DATABASE_URL="postgres://..."; npx prisma migrate dev --name init
#      Commit the generated prisma/migrations/ folder, then run
#      `npm run db:migrate` and `npm run db:seed` the same way (the seed wipes
#      and loads the demo fleet, and refuses NODE_ENV=production unless
#      ALLOW_PRODUCTION_SEED=true).
#   6. npm run build:cf   -> npm run preview:cf (optional local check)
#      -> npm run deploy:cf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (required for durable production storage; leave unset locally)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL connection string for Prisma (driver-adapter / Rust-free client,
# so it runs inside a Worker). Use a POOLED connection string — Neon's pooled
# endpoint or Supabase's "Transaction" pooler — since the Worker opens a
# short-lived connection per request, which an unpooled database can't
# sustain under load. (Cloudflare Hyperdrive isn't wired up: it supplies its
# connection string through a binding object rather than a string secret, so
# it would need a wrangler.jsonc binding plus a lib/db.ts change.)
# Production: `npx wrangler secret put` only.
# Locally, leave it unset to run against the zero-config data/db.json store
# (no database needed for `npm run dev` or CI).
DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public (client + server) configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical production URL — backs metadataBase for every absolute link in
# page metadata (canonical tags, OpenGraph/Twitter image URLs). Must be set
# at BUILD time (checklist step 4). Falls back to https://modfemautos.com if
# unset, so set it explicitly for any non-production deploy (e.g. staging),
# or social previews and canonical tags will point at the wrong place.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Fallback CAD -> NGN exchange rate used whenever the live /api/fx rate is
# unreachable. Defaults to 1180 if unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_FX_RATE=1180

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only configuration — never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_, since
# that inlines the value into the client JS bundle for anyone to read.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Passcode for the /admin dealer console. Required — there is no default, so
# /admin stays locked until this is set. Production: `npx wrangler secret put
# ADMIN_SECRET`. Local `next dev`: fill it in here once this file is copied
# to .env.development.local.
ADMIN_SECRET=
